{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{4}=25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}=25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{3}{4}\\alpha -\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(\\alpha -\\frac{3}{4}\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}\\alpha -\\beta =25\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ \\alpha -\\frac{3}{4}\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-12$ and $\\beta =-16.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=15\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =1$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(2\\beta -4\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-2\\alpha -4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-4\\alpha +2\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -4\\beta -2\\alpha =1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},$ $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+10y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+31\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+10y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+31\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+2(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+10(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+31\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +6\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+(-6\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+31\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha +6\\beta =1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ -6\\alpha +\\beta =31\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-5$ and $\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{3x}+3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=13\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -2)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =2$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $13\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)-4(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=13\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(-5\\alpha -12\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+(12\\alpha -5\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x=13\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5\\alpha -12\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ 12\\alpha -5\\beta =13\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{12}{13}$ and $\\beta =-\\frac{5}{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{12}{13}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{5}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x}+\\frac{12}{13}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{5}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256"