} {"question" "q-64272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ So we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-2\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -2\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =0$ and $\\beta =-1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-64272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9y=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+3x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =6(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)-9x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n6(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)-9x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+9x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-6\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+6\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6\\beta =-6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ -6\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =0$ and $\\beta =-1.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the  equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{2i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$ \n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4\\beta =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -4\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\beta =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solutionto the problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & =8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+16x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\,=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+8\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}8\\beta =16\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ -8\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1$ and $\\beta =2.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)=-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{-4x}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{-4x}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+16x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\,=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+8\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ -8\\alpha =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2}$, $\\beta =0.$\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+25y=-20\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x,$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)+5x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =10(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)-25x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n10(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)-25x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)+25x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)=-20\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-10\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+10\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡5x=-20\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10\\beta =-20\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x) \\\\ -10\\alpha =-10\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =-2.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}_{p}=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x"] ["math" "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,\\,y(0)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +1)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2(-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+(-4\\alpha -3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=-25\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha +4\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -4\\alpha -3\\beta =-25\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =4$ and $\\beta =3.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+4 & =4 \\\\ A & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-x}-Bx{e}^{-x}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A+B+6 & =0 \\\\ B & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=0,B=-6.$\n\nSo, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-6x{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-6x{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{-x}+6x{e}^{-x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=4{e}^{-x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=6{e}^{-x}+12x{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "y=6{e}^{-x}-{e}^{x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-6x{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=-25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{2x}+Bx{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=-25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & =A{e}^{2(0)}+B(0){e}^{2(0)}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\ -3 & =A-3 \\\\ A & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2A{e}^{2x}+2Bx{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=5$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =2A{e}^{2(0)}+2B(0){e}^{2(0)}+B{e}^{2(0)}+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\ 5 & =2A+B+4 \\\\ 5 & =2(0)+B+4 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=0$ and $B=1,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny=x{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=-5x{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=-x{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "y=x{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x{e}^{2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9y=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+3x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ {y}^{″} & =6(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+9x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n6(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+9x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+9x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-6\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+6\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ -6\\alpha =-12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =2,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+x(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=5.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+x(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n3Q+2=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P=2,Q=1.$\n\nSo, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-64228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-5y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,\\,y(0)=-\\frac{2}{5},\\,{y}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-5y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-5$ or $\\lambda =1$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ {y}^{″} & =-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+4(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)-5(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n(-14\\alpha +12\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+(-14\\beta -12\\alpha )\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-14\\alpha +12\\beta =1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x) \\\\ -14\\beta -12\\alpha =-4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{10},\\beta =\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=-\\frac{2}{5}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{10}.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{10}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-5A+B=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -5A+B=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=0,$ $B=-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-5x}+3{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-5x}-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] ["math" "y=\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5x}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-8110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =A{e}^{-2(0)}+B(0){e}^{-2(0)}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0) \\\\ -1 & =A-2 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}-2Bx{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =-2A{e}^{-2(0)}-2B(0){e}^{-2(0)}+B{e}^{-2(0)}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0) \\\\ -2 & =-2A+B \\\\ -2 & =-2+B \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=0,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0dbfff82362a24de20c408a502317aa9acc12c62643cf2cf1feb241677500ad"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-{e}^{-2x}+x{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{-2x}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x}+x{e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x}-4x{e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "q-93833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/state.json" "file_sha256" "52450302c051d76c96695501ed6ecbace02a4a72cb43ccf8f2a6887ab37cb49f"} {"question" "e-6612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6e4e0c7cab964302651798fb741f1144f92f6e2e57e65101a7943111932fdbbd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6612.json" "file_sha256" "4305ab11723ba787c6ca56fe1b3df9d89a01007639f6ac70e0fdfe0e8e649b00"} {"question" "e-6612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/a397e1a4149f4b6081f65d95f04741e60e2bd31fca19d3f8e09ed0f76db581de.png) so the complementary solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/c970482f98369bea187d9d95494395b7ddc3777c96c6f70928f5f7b2aae5f3b7.png)\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/d0cdd6ff1b44946ac1e910d23f7f40b83908992acbdba94329de63b7ee2c8f49.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/7ffc37c1e99b8efa7829e449730a07f729b1089965446233266d7b7b26d0ce90.png) is not a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/9f015e4ef6033cdc7ac1ff0de31ac36bf8d47b6fa702b773c32abc955bdb0d2f.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6709a006285d5cd34ad5d0cc38c5a301ee5e685991d0a63609d33e3dc9273524.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/b4c9f2e8e219faee88048f605f5ecf0957d84ed21896bbee9b25e7cb2953364d.png) are constants to be determined.\n\n**Caution:** The terms of the complementary solution are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/c1e8f4a9b683824e14a5b29e1bb1f23a90c03f90929c1ac8d04a3f2ba78d4c74.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/373d49e91c81adc100005e789dec85074254a9692d7858313966c886b589ec58.png) Although ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/16099b9989ef712e435b858d14cb006c5e62362412ae1b0e42e8025290dc644c.png) appears, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/669043a118b0a018e699c203330af94918b1df9744a2d9c6e04109e4ca39499a.png) is not itself a term because it is multiplied by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6b761e20295ebe1f6a5edf87ae5b7e480485dafbc0e623f4fab18efe2b8859c6.png)\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6316c498377eadd30922f7f5ef6cfa1015cb3c059349bccf2aec7ca52ea5356e.png) we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/48db0d80886317e03b0a772e8f36255308c9e1f8bac5824231981366a39e96f5.png)\n\nTo find the values of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6053d6cf8a3a4f931034631411cd2b07f16470ea835ae768c5783b33e0d18d55.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/f00a9053a63ce88c1749e8ce7fb389b3618c6e3d4be6a4a03b7031759fe62940.png) we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/e43bebbc4a12d780e880c4aa2fbb6f09f74e388163648858c95b0f2969d9168d.png)\n\nThe corresponding terms on both sides should have the same coefficients. Equating the coefficients of like terms, we get the following system:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/5f5871fd2c97ac62a9143268e844d0b0b0482ef93e8841138b5d0e6d08bf911f.png)\n\nSolving this system gives ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/bb5b3d4d7afe88b271c5feb2d48e9a5680c728cf6f33396eb4f226ad9bc4f3ff.png)\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/03049680a7f1934e4eb0a7031d73baf4789ee549f4495c563739dfe91ad1d19a.png)\nand the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/assets/6d839822be46648100d639e231ca1b4afe9460d4dec7b6a17c761f25475be381.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6612.json" "file_sha256" "4305ab11723ba787c6ca56fe1b3df9d89a01007639f6ac70e0fdfe0e8e649b00"} {"question" "e-6613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6613.json" "file_sha256" "eb0245e8c7536c08b45d17ed165cad2b53369f74654f0b6ea73b08034fad807a"} {"question" "e-6613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots $\\lambda = \\pm 2 \\textrm{i},$ so the complementary solution is \n\n$$\ny_c = A\\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution $y_p(x).$\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $4 \\sin 2x,$ and $\\sin 2x$ is a term in the complementary solution. So, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos{2x} + \\beta \\sin{2x}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x), \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta,$ we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ -4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -4\\alpha =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha = -1$ and $\\beta = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = -x \\cos{2x},\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={y}_{c}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6613.json" "file_sha256" "eb0245e8c7536c08b45d17ed165cad2b53369f74654f0b6ea73b08034fad807a"} {"question" "e-6788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x) = A \\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x} - x \\cos{2x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x, \\qquad y(0) = 2 , \\ \\ y'(0) = -3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6788.json" "file_sha256" "a8cec20cf477f535ab8d51e059335fa31f24eb6908ff57850590c875d4f95502"} {"question" "e-6788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\ 2 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-2A\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2B\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =-2A\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2B\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y'(0)=-3$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & =-2A\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2B\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+2(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\ -3 & =2B-1 \\\\ -2 & =2B \\\\ -1 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=-1,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065513/example-6788.json" "file_sha256" "a8cec20cf477f535ab8d51e059335fa31f24eb6908ff57850590c875d4f95502"}] "usage" {"q-8112" [] "q-8120" [] "e-6788" [] "q-8114" [] "q-64228" [] "e-6613" [] "e-6612" [] "q-64275" []} "basis" 2150 "retractions" [[17592186088337 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the problem\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 2\\frac{dy}{dx} - 3y = 2\\cos x + \\sin x$."] [17592186088169 :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 9y =-6\\cos 3x$\nhas the complementary function $y_{c}(x) = A\\cos 3x + B\\sin 3x$, find the particular solution $y_{p}(x)$ to this equation."] [17592186088339 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 4y = 8\\cos 2x - \\sin 2x$."] [17592186088338 :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$y^{″} + 2y^{′} + y =-25\\sin 2x, y(0) = 4, y^{′}(0) = 0$."] [17592186088167 :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$y^{″} + 9y = 6\\cos 3x - 12\\sin 3x, y(0) = 2, y^{′}(0) = 5$."] [17592186087545 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} - 4 \\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} + 5y = \\sin x$."] [17592186087545 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots\n\n$$\n\\lambda = 2 \\pm \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nso the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c = e^{2x}(A\\cos{x} +B\\sin{x})\n$$\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $\\sin x$, and $\\sin x$ is not a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form\n\n$$\ny_c = \\alpha \\cos{x} + \\beta \\sin{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are constants to be determined.\n\n**Caution:** The terms of the complementary solution are $A e^{2x} \\cos x$ and $B e^{2x} \\sin x$. Although $\\sin x$ appears, $\\sin x$ is not itself a term because it is multiplied by $e^{2x}$.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy_{p}}{dx} &= - α\\sin x + β\\cos x, \\\\\n\\frac{d^{2}y_{p}}{dx^{2}} &= - α\\cos x - β\\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(- α\\cos x - β\\sin x) - 4(- α\\sin x + β\\cos x) + 5(α\\cos x + β\\sin x) &= \\sin x \\\\\n(4α - 4β)\\cos x + (4α + 4β)\\sin x &= \\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding terms on both sides should have the same coefficients. Equating the coefficients of like terms, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{4α - 4β = 0\\begin{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\cos x) \\\\ 4α + 4β = 1\\end{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\sin x)\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives\n\n$$\n\\alpha= \\beta = \\dfrac 1 8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = \\dfrac{1}{8} \\cos {x} + \\dfrac{1}{8} \\sin {x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= y_{c}(x) + y_{p}(x) \\\\\n&= e^{2x}(A\\cos x + B\\sin x) + \\frac{1}{8}\\cos x + \\frac{1}{8}\\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087546 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x$."] [17592186087546 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the complementary solution by solving the associated homogeneous ODE. The characteristic equation has roots\n\n$$\n\\lambda = \\pm 2 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nso the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c = A\\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution $y_p(x)$.\n\nSecond, we find a particular solution of the inhomogeneous ODE. We see that the right-hand side is $4 \\sin 2x$, and $\\sin 2x$ is a term in the complementary solution. So, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos{2x} + \\beta \\sin{2x})\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are constants that are to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of $y_p$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy_{p}}{dx} &= (α\\cos 2x + β\\sin 2x) + 2x(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x), \\\\\n\\frac{d^{2}y_{p}}{dx^{2}} &= 4(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x) + 4x(- α\\cos 2x - β\\sin 2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we substitute the derivatives into the original ODE and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(- α\\sin 2x + β\\cos 2x) + 4x(- α\\cos 2x - β\\sin 2x) + 4x(α\\cos 2x + β\\sin 2x) &= 4\\sin 2x \\\\\n- 4α\\sin 2x + 4β\\cos 2x &= 4\\sin 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{4β = 0\\begin{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\cos 2x) \\\\ -4α = 4\\end{vmatrix}(equating the coefficients of\\sin 2x)\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha = -1$ and $\\beta = 0$.\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = -x \\cos{2x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= y_{c} + y_{p} \\\\\n&= A\\cos 2x + B\\sin 2x - x\\cos 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087554 :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x$\nhas the general solution\n$y(x) = A \\cos{2x} + B \\sin{2x} - x \\cos{2x}$,\nsolve the initial value problem\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + 4y = 4\\sin 2x, \\qquad y(0) = 2, \\ \\ y'(0) = -3$."] [17592186087554 :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n$2|= A\\cos 0 + B\\sin 0 - 0\\cos 0; 2|= A$.\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n$y^{′}|=-2A\\sin 2x + 2B\\cos 2x - (\\cos 2x - 2x\\sin 2x); =-2A\\sin 2x + 2B\\cos 2x - \\cos 2x + 2x\\sin 2x$.\nSubstituting $y'(0)=-3$ into the derivative gives\n$-3|=-2A\\sin 0 + 2B\\cos 0 - \\cos 0 + 2(0)\\sin 0; - 3|= 2B - 1; - 2|= 2B; - 1|= B$.\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=-1$, we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny = 2\\cos 2x - \\sin 2x - x\\cos 2x\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186085934 17592186085935 17592186085936 17592186085937 17592186085938 17592186085946 17592186085947 17592186085948 17592186085949 17592186085950 17592186086953 17592186086954 17592186086955 17592186086956 17592186086957 17592186086959 17592186086960 17592186086961 17592186086962 17592186086963 17592186086965 17592186086966 17592186086967 17592186086968 17592186086969] "immutable_fields" [[17592186085933 :answer-field/correct] [17592186085933 :answer-field/id] [17592186085933 :answer-field/key] [17592186085933 :answer-field/type] [17592186085945 :answer-field/correct] [17592186085945 :answer-field/id] [17592186085945 :answer-field/key] [17592186085945 :answer-field/type] [17592186086952 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086952 :answer-field/id] [17592186086952 :answer-field/key] [17592186086952 :answer-field/type] [17592186086958 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086958 :answer-field/id] [17592186086958 :answer-field/key] [17592186086958 :answer-field/type] [17592186086964 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086964 :answer-field/id] [17592186086964 :answer-field/key] [17592186086964 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
